{"basis": 3425, "questions": [[{":db/id": 17592186096417, ":knowledge-point/_canonical-example": [{":db/id": 17592186096617, ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}], ":question/id": "d7a77a89-0535-54da-a246-36ee5b4e9e7f", ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3634", ":question/problem": "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$", ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}], [{":db/id": 17592186235429, ":knowledge-point/_questions": [{":db/id": 17592186059675, ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions"}], ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "f82a959f-469c-580d-b699-744a01e1a73e", ":answer/type": {":db/id": 17592186045498, ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"}, ":answer/value": "-4\\operatorname{cos}x", ":db/id": 17592186234938}], ":answer-field/correct": {":answer/id": "f82a959f-469c-580d-b699-744a01e1a73e", ":answer/type": {":db/id": 17592186045498, ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"}, ":answer/value": "-4\\operatorname{cos}x", ":db/id": 17592186234938}, ":answer-field/id": "01d3bdac-6753-510d-b7d4-b1bb408d2f9f", ":answer-field/key": "field-1", ":answer-field/type": {":db/id": 17592186045492, ":db/ident": ":answer-field.type/blank"}, ":db/id": 17592186234978}], ":question/difficulty": {":db/id": 17592186045485, ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"}, ":question/id": "8a37e3e9-7f1b-5a8d-b564-d8b93eaac32a", ":question/math-academy-id": "q-167324", ":question/problem": "$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=${{field-1}}", ":step/_content": [{":db/id": 17592186235739, ":step/id": "c2